#lang saffron
;; saffron-effect-row-lost-through-unannotated-call, the half that is fixed.
;;
;; `(+ (g) 1)` in a Saffron file puts the call to `g` inside a DYNAMIC OPERATOR
;; node, and every structural walk in src/passes/effect_check.c lacked an arm
;; for those nodes -- so it fell to `default` and stopped.  The caller's
;; inferred effect row came back empty, and an enclosing handler was reported
;; unreachable (TUR-W0033: "the body does not perform 'Ask'") before the
;; program aborted.  The same walk in src/passes/cps.c had the same gap, so the
;; caller was never colored either.
;;
;; Both are fixed, and under `--interpret` this program now prints the right
;; answers.  THE COMPILED BACK END STILL ABORTS on the same program, for a
;; separate reason that is not the effect row: the CPS IR delegates a dynamic
;; node's whole subtree to the direct emitter on `!operand_uses_control`, which
;; asks about lexical control OPERATORS and not about calls to effectful
;; FUNCTIONS -- so the delegated region calls `g()`'s direct entry, which opens
;; a fresh DK root.  That is why this fixture is `requires.interp-only`: the
;; compiled arm is still open, and the report says so.
;;
;; The report's own hypothesis -- that `any` carries no row, so the row was lost
;; through the unannotated RETURN -- was wrong.  `straight` below is the control
;; that says so: the identical call chain with no dynamic operator between the
;; handler and the perform has always worked, with every signature just as
;; unannotated.

(defeffect Ask [] : int)

(defn g [] (perform (Ask)))

;; The control: no dynamic node between `handle` and `perform`.
(defn straight [] (g))

;; The repro: `+` on an `any` is a dynamic op, so the call to `g` sits under it.
(defn through-op [] (+ (g) 1))

;; ...and through a COMPARISON, which is a different dynamic operator reaching
;; the same arm, so the fix is not keyed to arithmetic.
(defn through-cmp [] (> (g) 0))

;; NOT here, deliberately: the same comparison inside an `if`
;; (`(if (> (g) 0) 1 0)`) still loses the row, and a `(Box (g))` constructor
;; argument loses it in PLAIN TURMERIC too.  Both are residues of the same
;; species in other walks, recorded in the report rather than pinned here --
;; a fixture that asserts a wrong answer is worse than no fixture.

(defn main []
  (println (handle (straight)    (Ask [] k) (resume k 41)))
  (println (handle (through-op)  (Ask [] k) (resume k 41)))
  (println (handle (through-cmp) (Ask [] k) (resume k 41)))
  0)
